                <pb facs="0728" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg658"/>

                <head>No. 409.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 19, 1883</date>.
                        (Received July 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 646.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Mexican Congress adjourned yesterday.
                    The important work done during the session was: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Making an appropriation for the expenses of a legation at
                            London.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Authorizing a settlement of the public debt.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Authorizing the President to contract a loan of twenty millions of
                            dollars.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
